    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d584">

                <pb facs="0639" n="629" sameAs="frus:frus1944v04/pg629"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00112 European War 1939/8–2444:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Sweden</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stockholm</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-08-24T19:00:00+01:00">August 24, 1944—7
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 8:36 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3284. Legation’s 3270, August 24, 3 p.m. Madame Kollontay has just advised me
                    that she saw Foreign Minister Günther this afternoon and fully supported our <hi
                        rendition="#italic">démarche</hi>. She described Mr. Günther’s reaction as
                    “not unfavorable”.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
